            <ArticleTitle>[Exercise treatment in vertebragenic headache: (author's transl)].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>469-72</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>In treating vertebragenic headache, the segmental movement, the shortened postural muscles, the feeble phasic muscles and the wrong patterns of movement can be influenced by exercises. The techniques of some of these exercises are described, the importance of an exact diagnosis is pointed out.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
